Task — calculate the correlation

Using your covariance from two slides ago, and the SD of each variable: calculate the correlation coefficient.



{
  const rows = student_summary.filter(d =&gt; d.finger_mm != null && !isNaN(d.finger_mm))
  if (rows.length &lt; 3) return html`&lt;p style="color:#aaa;"&gt;Will compute automatically once enough data is in.&lt;/p&gt;`
  const xs = rows.map(d =&gt; d.finger_mm), ys = rows.map(d =&gt; d.mean_rt)
  const mx = d3.mean(xs), my = d3.mean(ys)
  const cov = d3.mean(xs.map((x,i) =&gt; (x - mx) * (ys[i] - my)))
  const corr = cov / (d3.deviation(xs) * d3.deviation(ys))
  return html`&lt;p style="font-family:sans-serif;"&gt;Corr[finger length, reaction time] = &lt;strong style="color:#e63946;font-size:1.2em;"&gt;${corr.toFixed(2)}&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;`
}








