{
  const rows = student_summary.filter(d =&gt; d.finger_mm != null && !isNaN(d.finger_mm))
  if (rows.length &lt; 3) return html`&lt;p style="color:#aaa;"&gt;Not enough data yet.&lt;/p&gt;`
  // True beta* and Var[x*] from our real, unperturbed data — fixed throughout
  const xbar = d3.mean(rows, d =&gt; d.finger_mm), ybar = d3.mean(rows, d =&gt; d.mean_rt)
  const cov = d3.mean(rows, d =&gt; (d.finger_mm - xbar) * (d.mean_rt - ybar))
  const varXStar = d3.mean(rows, d =&gt; (d.finger_mm - xbar) ** 2)
  const trueBeta = cov / varXStar
  // The formula from the previous slide: beta = beta* x Var[x*] / (Var[x*] + Var[e])
  // This ratio is always in (0, 1], so beta can shrink toward zero but can never cross it.
  const betaFor = sd =&gt; trueBeta * (varXStar / (varXStar + sd ** 2))
  const currentBeta = betaFor(noiseSD)
  const curve = d3.range(0, 10.2, 0.2).map(sd =&gt; ({ sd, beta: betaFor(sd) }))
  const chart = Plot.plot({
    height: 350, marginLeft: 60,
    x: { label: "extra noise SD added to finger length (mm)" },
    y: { label: "attenuated β̂" },
    marks: [
      Plot.ruleY([0], { stroke: "#ccc" }),
      Plot.line(curve, { x: "sd", y: "beta", stroke: "#457b9d", strokeWidth: 2 }),
      Plot.dot([{ sd: noiseSD, beta: currentBeta }], { x: "sd", y: "beta", fill: "#e63946", r: 6 }),
    ]
  })
  return html`&lt;div&gt;${chart}&lt;p style="font-family:sans-serif;font-size:1em;text-align:center;"&gt;β̂* with no extra noise: &lt;strong&gt;${trueBeta.toFixed(3)}&lt;/strong&gt; &nbsp;·&nbsp; attenuated β̂ at current noise: &lt;strong&gt;${currentBeta.toFixed(3)}&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;`
}







\(\hat\beta\) shrinks toward zero as noise is added to finger length — but it never crosses zero, no matter how much noise is added. \(Var[x^*]/(Var[x^*]+Var[e])\) is always between 0 and 1, so attenuation can flatten the line but can never flip its sign.

Task — SE and CI for our own regression

By hand or in Excel: using the SE(β̂) formula from the last slide and β̂ from Week 4, calculate the 95% CI for our own finger-length regression.



{
  const rows = student_summary.filter(d =&gt; d.finger_mm != null && !isNaN(d.finger_mm))
  if (rows.length &lt; 4) return html`&lt;p style="color:#aaa;"&gt;Not enough data yet.&lt;/p&gt;`
  const x = rows.map(d =&gt; d.finger_mm), y = rows.map(d =&gt; d.mean_rt)
  const n = x.length
  const xbar = d3.mean(x), ybar = d3.mean(y)
  const cov = d3.mean(x.map((xi, i) =&gt; (xi - xbar) * (y[i] - ybar)))
  const varx = d3.mean(x.map(xi =&gt; (xi - xbar) ** 2))
  const beta = cov / varx, alpha = ybar - beta * xbar
  const resid = x.map((xi, i) =&gt; y[i] - (alpha + beta * xi))
  const sdE = Math.sqrt(d3.sum(resid.map(e =&gt; e ** 2)) / (n - 2))
  const sdX = Math.sqrt(varx)
  const seBeta = sdE / (Math.sqrt(n) * sdX)
  const lo = beta - 2 * seBeta, hi = beta + 2 * seBeta
  return html`&lt;p style="font-family:sans-serif;font-size:1.1em;"&gt;
    β̂ = &lt;strong&gt;${beta.toFixed(3)}&lt;/strong&gt; &nbsp;·&nbsp; SE(β̂) = &lt;strong&gt;${seBeta.toFixed(3)}&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
    95% CI: &lt;strong&gt;[${lo.toFixed(3)}, ${hi.toFixed(3)}]&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;`
}








